    "result": "## Summary\n\nI've successfully fixed the bug in the `frai gate init --ci` command. The issue was that the `--ci` flag, defined on the main `frai` command, wasn't being passed through to the spawned `frai-gate` CLI.\n\n**The Problem:**\n- The `--ci` flag is parsed by the parent `frai` command but wasn't being forwarded to the spawned child process\n- Only the subcommand's direct args were being passed to the gate CLI\n\n**The Fix (in `packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts`):**\nUpdated the gate command handler to:\n1. Accept the `command` parameter from Commander.js\n2. Extract the parent command's options using `command?.parent?.opts()`\n3. Reconstruct the full argument list including both subcommand args and parent command options before spawning the child process\n\n**Verification:**\n\u2705 Rebuilt with `pnpm --filter frai build`\n\u2705 Tested `frai gate init --ci` - now correctly creates both:\n  - `FRAI-SPEC.md`\n  - `.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml`",
